TERMS AND CONDITIONS

1. DEFINITIONS

   "Software" means DJView and its source code, object code, documentation,
   and all associated files covered by this license.

   "Derivative Work" means any work that is based on or incorporates any
   portion of the Software, including modifications, translations, adaptations,
   and works that link against or embed the Software.

   "Distribute" means to make the Software or a Derivative Work available to
   any third party, whether by download, physical media, network access,
   or any other means.

   "Network Use" means running the Software or a Derivative Work on a server
   or networked system such that other users can interact with it remotely.

2. GRANT OF RIGHTS

   Subject to the terms of this license, each contributor grants you a
   worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to:

   a) Use, copy, and study the Software for any purpose.
   b) Modify the Software and create Derivative Works.
   c) Distribute the Software and Derivative Works.

3. COPYLEFT REQUIREMENT

   Any Derivative Work you Distribute or make available via Network Use MUST:

   a) Be released in full under this exact license, without modification
      to the license terms.
   b) Include complete, buildable source code for the entire Derivative Work,
      made available at no charge, in a publicly accessible location.
   c) Prominently state that it is a Derivative Work of DJView and identify
      all significant modifications made.
   d) Retain all copyright notices, attribution notices, and this license
      in every copy and in any documentation.

   You may NOT sublicense, re-license, or impose any additional terms that
   restrict the rights granted herein.

4. NETWORK USE PROVISION

   If you operate a Derivative Work as a network service (including SaaS,
   cloud deployment, or any form of remote access), you MUST make the complete
   corresponding source code available to all users of that service, under
   this license, at no charge. A publicly accessible source repository
   satisfies this requirement.

5. NO REDISTRIBUTION RESTRICTIONS

   You may NOT use any legal mechanism — including but not limited to trademark
   rights, patent rights, subscription agreements, terms of service, or
   end-user license agreements — to restrict any recipient's ability to:

   a) Redistribute the Software or Derivative Work in source or binary form.
   b) Build the Software from source.
   c) Exercise any right granted by this license.

   This provision specifically closes the practice of distributing GPL-licensed
   source while using trademark or subscription terms to prevent redistribution
   of compiled binaries (sometimes referred to as the "Red Hat loophole").

6. ANTI-TIVOIZATION

   If you Distribute the Software or a Derivative Work in or alongside hardware
   that restricts the installation or execution of modified versions (e.g.,
   through hardware signature verification or secure boot lockout), you MUST
   also provide the information or keys necessary for users to install and run
   modified versions on that hardware.

7. PATENTS

   Each contributor grants you a royalty-free, worldwide, non-exclusive patent
   license under the contributor's essential patent claims, solely to the extent
   necessary to exercise the rights granted by this license. If you initiate
   patent litigation against any party alleging that the Software infringes a
   patent, your license from that contributor terminates immediately.

8. SOURCE CODE AVAILABILITY

   When you Distribute a Derivative Work in binary or compiled form, you MUST
   simultaneously make the complete corresponding source code available, either:

   a) By including it in the same distribution, or
   b) By providing a written offer, valid for at least three years, to supply
      the source code to any third party who requests it at no charge, or
   c) By publishing it in a publicly accessible version control repository
      and including the URL in the distribution.

9. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTY

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
